{
  "company_name": "LabAuto Sciences",
  "industry": "Chemicals & Materials",
  "use_case": "Autonomous lab experiment tracking and formulation optimization",
  "space_title": "LabAuto Sciences - Autonomous Lab Experiments & Optimization \ud83e\uddea",
  "space_description": "**Subindustry:** Chemicals & Materials\n\n**Use case:** Autonomous Lab Experiments & Formulation Optimization\n\nLabAuto Sciences \u2014 model-guided high-throughput experimentation across 20 formulation targets (catalysts, coatings, polymers, pharmaceuticals, nanomaterials) at 4 global labs. The R&D VP uses this space to rank formulations by yield headroom and program ROI; bench scientists track pass rate and model accuracy to decide when to trust the recommender; the CFO watches cost per experiment and time-to-lead-candidate (autonomous labs typically cut cycle time 5-10x versus manual workflows).\n\n**Key KPIs**\n- Average product yield (%) \u2014 primary R&D outcome; best-in-class catalysts run 70-90%\n- Experiment pass rate (%) \u2014 share of runs hitting spec; target 75-85%\n- Average product purity (%) \u2014 release-gate indicator; typical 95-99% for specialty chemicals\n- Cost per experiment ($) \u2014 efficiency benchmark; autonomous platforms run $200-$5,000/run\n- Model prediction accuracy (%) \u2014 closeness of predicted to actual yield; target \u2265 85%\n- Yield headroom (best_yield - avg_yield) \u2014 optimization potential per formulation\n- Total experiments run \u2014 throughput; healthy autonomous lab targets 20-50 runs/week\n- Model confidence score \u2014 gates which recommendations get auto-executed (\u2265 0.85 typical)\n\n**Data sources**\n- `experiment_runs` \u2014 daily run-level data with parameters (T, P, time), yield, purity, pass/fail\n- `parameter_snapshots` \u2014 weekly model-recommended optimal settings and confidence per formulation\n- `optimization_monthly` \u2014 monthly KPI rollups: pass rate, average yield, cost per experiment, model accuracy",
  "schema_basename": "auto_lab_experiments",
  "tables": [
    {
      "table_name": "experiment_runs",
      "description": "Individual experiment run records with formulation, parameters, measured outcomes, and pass/fail results from autonomous lab systems.",
      "columns": [
        {
          "name": "run_id",
          "sql_type": "STRING",
          "comment": "Unique experiment run identifier",
          "is_dimension": false,
          "generation_expr": "CONCAT('RUN-', LPAD(CAST({id_seq} AS STRING), 5, '0'))"
        },
        {
          "name": "run_date",
          "sql_type": "DATE",
          "comment": "Date experiment was executed",
          "is_dimension": false,
          "generation_expr": "dt"
        },
        {
          "name": "formulation_id",
          "sql_type": "STRING",
          "comment": "Target formulation identifier",
          "is_dimension": true,
          "generation_expr": ""
        },
        {
          "name": "formulation_name",
          "sql_type": "STRING",
          "comment": "Human-readable formulation name",
          "is_dimension": true,
          "generation_expr": ""
        },
        {
          "name": "formulation_category",
          "sql_type": "STRING",
          "comment": "Category: Catalysts, Coatings, Polymers, Pharmaceuticals, Nanomaterials",
          "is_dimension": true,
          "generation_expr": ""
        },
        {
          "name": "lab_facility",
          "sql_type": "STRING",
          "comment": "Lab facility where experiment ran",
          "is_dimension": false,
          "generation_expr": "CASE WHEN {status_noise} < 0.25 THEN 'Lab-Boston' WHEN {status_noise} < 0.50 THEN 'Lab-SanDiego' WHEN {status_noise} < 0.75 THEN 'Lab-Basel' ELSE 'Lab-Shanghai' END"
        },
        {
          "name": "temperature_c",
          "sql_type": "DOUBLE",
          "comment": "Reaction temperature in Celsius",
          "is_dimension": false,
          "generation_expr": "ROUND(25 + {qty_noise} * 475, 1)"
        },
        {
          "name": "pressure_bar",
          "sql_type": "DOUBLE",
          "comment": "Reaction pressure in bar",
          "is_dimension": false,
          "generation_expr": "ROUND(1.0 + {qty_noise} * 49.0, 2)"
        },
        {
          "name": "reaction_time_minutes",
          "sql_type": "DOUBLE",
          "comment": "Reaction duration in minutes",
          "is_dimension": false,
          "generation_expr": "ROUND(5 + {qty_noise} * 355, 1)"
        },
